# Ashling's Command, modes 3 and 4: "Ashling's Command deals 2 damage to each creature target player controls" and "Target player
# creates two Treasure tokens". Bot1 targets Bot2 for the damage: Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2) dies and its Picklock Prankster (1/3)
# survives with 2 damage; Bot1's own Ornithopter is not "a creature target player controls" and is untouched. Bot1 targets itself
# for the Treasures and gets two Treasure tokens (CR 111.10a), both at once; Bot2 gets none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Ashling's Command
Ornithopter
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Picklock Prankster
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Picklock Prankster.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ashling's Command.Cast
Bot1.Modes(3; 4)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Picklock Prankster
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Picklock Prankster.Damage = 2
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby; Ornithopter; Treasure Token; Treasure Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#1.Token = true
Stack.Count = 0
